# Attention
# 1. Tokenization and Embedding
# 2. X- embedding vector we calculate QXW, KXW, VXW so XW are learnable parameters
# 3. we [get qit,kit,vit],[qcat,kcat,vcat] for every token
# 4. We are peocessing it: query: what info do I need to understand myself?
# 5. Qit goes against all the Keys and generate relevance score which are not proabilities. they are just similarity scores
    # Qit · Kit        = 0.7
    # Qit · Kwas       = 0.4
    # Qit · Khungry    = 5.7
# Scaling: Because if Q and K are large-dimensional vectors, their dot products can become large. Softmax would become extremely sharp. so we didvide by sqrt(dk​) to get more manageble range.
# Calculate Attention Weights (probability) using the Softmax[using activation function I convert them to probability]
# Softmax converts the relevance scores into normalized attention weights.
# Now retrieve information from V
    # Attention weights:

    # cat       0.70
    # milk      0.05
    # hungry    0.20
    # others    0.05
# Output=0.70Vcat​+0.05Vmilk​+0.20Vhungry​+... [High Attention -- large multipler -- more value --more Value information included] [Low attention--small multiplier--little Value information included]
# The token with a high attention weight contributes more of its Value vector to the final output.
#                     ATTENTION FROM SCRATCH
#                             │
#         ┌───────────────────┼───────────────────┐
#         │                   │                   │
#    1. INPUT            2. Q K V             3. SCORES
#         │                   │                   │
#    Tokenization        Query (Q)          Q × Kᵀ
#         │               Key (K)                │
#    Embeddings           Value (V)         Scaling
#         │                   │             / √dₖ
#         │                   │                   │
#         └───────────────────┼───────────────────┘
#                             │
#                        4. SOFTMAX
#                             │
#                     Attention Weights
#                             │
#                             ▼
#                      5. WEIGHTED SUM
#                             │
#                        Weights × V
#                             │
#                             ▼
#                     6. ATTENTION OUTPUT
#                             │
#                             ▼
#                  7. VISUALIZATION
#                             │
#               ┌─────────────┼─────────────┐
#               │             │             │
#           Q/K/V Matrix   Score Matrix   Heatmap
#               │             │             │
#               └─────────────┼─────────────┘
#                             ▼
